# Global Claude Code defaults (example — copy to ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md)

These rules apply across every project unless a project's own CLAUDE.md
overrides them.

## Editing
- Prefer Edit over Write.
- Use absolute paths in tool calls.

## Comments
- Default to no comments. Only when the WHY is non-obvious.
- Never narrate WHAT — well-named identifiers do that.

## Destructive operations
- Always ask before: `rm`, `git reset --hard`, `git push --force`,
  dropping tables, deleting branches, killing processes.

## Communication
- Concise. Match length to task complexity.
- No emojis unless asked.
- Reference code as `path:line`.
